<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zheng family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zheng family was a maritime trading and military clan of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-zhilong">Zheng Zhilong</a> and his son Zheng Chenggong, known in the West as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a>. Remaining loyal to the Ming, they resisted the Qing conquest and in 1662 seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>. The Qing recovered Taiwan from the Zheng in 1683, completing their consolidation of China.</p></div>
